  "clause_1_scope": "This Indian Standard (IS 2347) covers Domestic Pressure Cooker - Specification. This Indian Standard (Fifth Revision) was adopted by the Utensils, Cutlery and Domestic Hardware Sectional Committee had been approved by the Mechanical Engineering Division Council, This standard was first published in 1963 and subsequently revised in 1966, 1974, 1987 and 1995. In this revision, following major changes have keen made: a) Amendment No. 1 has been incorporated, b) Handles and knobs shall conform to 'Performance of handless and handle assemblies attached to cookware — specification', c) Safety pressure relief device clause has been modified, and d) Test for spring loaded mechanism has been modified. The Committee responsible for the formulation of this standard is given at Annex J. For the purpose of deciding whether a particular requirement of this standard is complied with, t final value, observed or calculated, expressing the result of a test or analysis, shall be rounded off in accordance with 'Rules for rounding off numerical values {revised)' . The number of signif",
